Batocera only builds this ARMSX2 fork for one target: RK3588 boards
(4x Cortex-A76 + 4x Cortex-A55 big.LITTLE). The generic Linux/aarch64
branch here only requests "-march=armv8.1-a" (just enough for atomic
RMW instructions), leaving out A76-specific features like dot-product,
crypto, and full FP16 that Buildroot's own board-wide "-mtune=cortex-a76"
can't enable (mtune only affects scheduling, not which instructions the
compiler is allowed to emit).

"-mcpu=cortex-a76" already implies LSE atomics, so it satisfies the
original comment's requirement while also unlocking the rest of what
this core actually supports.

--- a/cmake/BuildParameters.cmake
+++ b/cmake/BuildParameters.cmake
@@ -119,7 +119,9 @@ elseif("${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR}" STREQUAL "arm64" OR "${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSO
 		add_compile_options("-march=armv8.4-a" "-mcpu=apple-m1")
 	else()
 		# Require atomic rmw instructions
-		add_compile_options("-march=armv8.1-a")
+		# batocera: target RK3588's Cortex-A76 cores specifically (implies LSE
+		# atomics, plus dotprod/crypto/fp16 that armv8.1-a alone doesn't enable)
+		add_compile_options("-mcpu=cortex-a76")
 	endif()

 	# If we're running on Linux, we need to detect the page/cache line size.
